.TH MAN 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
man \- lecteur de manuel / manual pager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man
[-k word | -f name | -w] [section] page...
.br
.B info
name
.br
.B apropos
word
.br
.B whatis
name
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats and displays manual pages found in /usr/share/man/LANG/manN and /usr/share/man/manN (or in the directories listed in MANPATH), where LANG is fr, en, de,
es or it according to the LANGUAGE setting. The roff macros TH SH SS B I BR RB IR RI BI IB P PP LP TP IP RS RE nf fi br sp and the fonts \\fB \\fI \\fR are
understood. When the output is a terminal the text goes through $PAGER (default less).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -k word
Search page names and descriptions (apropos).
.TP
.B -f name
Show the one line description of name (whatis).
.TP
.B -w
Print the path of the page instead of displaying it.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/man/man1/*.1, /usr/share/info/*
.SH SEE ALSO
less(1)
